# Code review ownership for touchstone itself.
# What adopters get is templates/github/CODEOWNERS, not this file.
#
# The kit's own advice (standards/practices/collaboration.md, standards/platform/ci-cd.md) is
# "key to TEAMS, not individuals, with a catch-all fallback". The team half of that advice is for
# multi-team product repos: touchstone is a single-maintainer standards repo with no GitHub org
# behind it, so there is no team to key to, and inventing one would produce lines GitHub silently
# ignores — the exact failure mode the template warns about. The catch-all is therefore keyed to
# the maintainer, and it is the whole file: path rules resolving to the same single owner would
# add review latency and no reviewer.
#
# Last match wins. Invalid lines are silently ignored, so verify this file renders owners in the
# PR sidebar after editing it, and keep "Require review from Code Owners" enabled in the branch
# ruleset protecting `main` — a CODEOWNERS file with no rule requiring its review is decoration.

# Catch-all fallback — every path, including ones added later.
